; XauUsdTradePreview v1.05 - READ-ONLY HISTORY_BRIDGE proof on the CURRENT demo (T012). Observation only: no order is sent, changed, cancelled or closed,
; and no new trade is needed. The EA reads the deal history and open positions of the robot's Tirane day (read-only) and feeds the bridge.
; WHAT THIS PRESET PROVES: with the history NOT asserted complete, no balance at the start of the day and the result formula / classification left UNSET,
; the bridge must BLOCK with concrete reasons and the daily check must NOT be called.
; BEFORE RUNNING: (1) set InpEntry / InpStopLoss to levels that pass the T008 checks for the CURRENT XAUUSD quote (the daily source is evaluated after
; the plan and the broker probe; if they stop first you see GEOMETRY / PLAN instead); (2) edit InpDailyEaMagic (a value > 0) and InpDailyServerOffsetSeconds
; (server time minus UTC, a multiple of 900; the history diagnostic prints TimeTradeServer()-TimeGMT()) to your demo values. The values below are
; PLACEHOLDERS, not facts: a different magic or offset only changes which deals are found; the expected reasons below do not depend on them.
; EXPECTED log line "T012 DAILY source=HISTORY_BRIDGE": history_verdict=READY (if the history is readable; otherwise UNKNOWN / BLOCK with a concrete
;   history_reason) allowed=0 primary=HISTORY_INCOMPLETE
;   reasons=HISTORY_INCOMPLETE|BALANCE_START_UNSET|POLICY_UNSET:result_formula|POLICY_UNSET:trade_classification daily_check_called=0
;   cancel_pending_due=0 daily_limit_reached=0, then T008 PREVIEW RESULT BLOCK with "DAILY: ..." in the reasons.
; TO SEE OTHER BLOCKS (one change at a time): InpDailyHistoryComplete=true removes HISTORY_INCOMPLETE; InpDailyBalanceStart=<balance at the start of the
; day> with InpDailySnapshotDay=<today yyyymmdd> removes BALANCE_START_UNSET; a wrong InpDailySnapshotDay gives BALANCE_DAY_MISMATCH; InpDailyResultFormula=NET
; gives POLICY_UNSUPPORTED:result_formula. Choosing a formula or a classification is a client / owner decision: nothing here suggests one.
; The preview uses TimeGMT() (PC clock) for the day and refuses the source in the Strategy Tester.
